{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>You shall rise before the hoary head.</b> Even an old man who is an ignoramus (am ha-aretz) — that is, a 'bor' (בור), as Targum renders לא תשם (Genesis 47) as לא תבור." "<b>And you shall honor the face of an elder.</b> Even a youth, if he is wise — as they said: 'elder (זקן)' means none other than one who has acquired wisdom, as it is said (Proverbs 8): ״ה' קנני ראשית דרכו״. And so is the view of the Targum, but it attached the wisdom to the word 'hoary head (שיבה),' for it translated מפני שיבה as מן קדם דסבר באורייתא — that is: 'You shall rise before the hoary head' — this is the Written Torah; 'and you shall honor the face of an elder' — this is the Oral Torah."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:12.740095001Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}